## PHASE 3 — Narrative Intelligence & Director Mode

**Goal:**
Upgrade from “similarity-based ordering” to **“narrative-aware storylines”** with roles, arcs, and explanations.

### Scope

1. Role classification (intro, buildup, climax, etc.)
2. Narrative arc scoring (energy curve)
3. Multiple storyline strategies
4. AI explanation of produced storyline

### AI Worker

* `apps/ai_worker/clipsense_worker/nlp/classification/role_classifier.py`
  Assigns each clip a “role” label.

* `apps/ai_worker/clipsense_worker/nlp/sentiment/analyzer.py`
  Detects emotional intensity / sentiment.

* `apps/ai_worker/clipsense_worker/story_engine/narrative_arc.py`
  Uses moods, sentiment, role to score energy/pacing.

* `apps/ai_worker/clipsense_worker/story_engine/storyline_generator.py`
  Extended to produce:

  * Narrative-focused storyline
  * High-energy-first
  * Emotion-driven variant

* `apps/ai_worker/clipsense_worker/story_engine/prompts.py`
  LLM prompts to generate human-readable “why this order works”.

* `apps/ai_worker/clipsense_worker/models/batch_analysis.py`
  Capture distributions: roles, moods, themes per batch.

### Backend

* `apps/api/internal/models/analysis.go`
  Extended to store role, mood, energy, etc.

* `apps/api/internal/models/storyline.go`
  Add: type (e.g. `balanced`, `high_energy`, `emotional`), explanation text.

* `apps/api/internal/http/handlers/storylines.go`
  `GET /storylines/{id}` -> include explanation + arc data.

### Frontend

* `apps/web/src/components/storylines/NarrativeArc.tsx`
  Draw energy curve across the clip order.

* `apps/web/src/components/storylines/StorylineEditor.tsx`
  Show explanation, allow reordering, inspect clips in context.

* `apps/web/src/components/batch/BatchOverview.tsx`
  Integrate batch-level insights: role distribution, mood distribution.

